rules:['Exactly3 token IDs partition into free/reserved/recovering. Reserving2 in a covenant leaves at most1 free token. No kills, observed dice or damage generate new threads.','Tie1 AP reserves1/uses1; Covenant2 AP reserves2/uses2. Consent from both endpoints; source may be caster, endpoints distinct. Each endpoint within30ft on formation, ≤60ft apart on maintenance. Expiry end of second subsequent caster turn.','Use the post-mitigation/pre-temp partition in sharedR1: bearer getsmin(3,D), protected D−that. Transferred burden is not re-mitigated, cannot trigger links/gains or recursively loop. Assigned damage is conserved, actual clamped HP loss need not equal it.','Covenant holds both tokens through first use. On final use or Cut/Sever closure tokens enter recovering until their caster’s next own turn. Unused natural expiry releasesfree; encounter closure releases only after pending events settle.','Cut Clean1 AP only your own existing link. Sever2 AP prices one free thread into recovery and removes only an identified registered fate-link object within30ft; unrelated buffs, gods, bloodlines or ordinary relationships are ineligible. Enemy’s reserved tokens recover on its own next turn.','Reanchor1 AP changes exactly one endpoint with consent/range checks, preserving original event/use/expiry. Cannot occur once the trigger begins. No use/expiry refresh from cycling endpoints.','Only one link per original event: earliest accepted room creation sequence wins across casters; other links are not consumed. An invalid/dead/retired/out-of-range endpoint ends eligibility before partition; normal original damage remains. No after-receipt damage rewrite.'],
